---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Statement from '../components/Statement.astro';
import { business } from '../data/business';

const title = 'About — Wardith';
const description =
  'Wardith is a small UK business that helps service firms get found when their customers ask AI assistants who to use. Plain pricing, no guarantees we can’t keep, no invented results.';
---

<Base title={title} description={description}>
  <section class="hero hero--rules">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h1>What is Wardith?</h1>
      <p class="lede" data-reveal>
        A small business with one job: making sure that when your customers ask an AI assistant to
        recommend someone who does what you do, your name is in the answer.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap split split--sticky">
      <div data-reveal>
        <h2>Why does Wardith exist?</h2>
      </div>
      <div data-reveal>
        <p>
          Because something is changing that most businesses can't see. People now ask ChatGPT,
          Google, Copilot or Perplexity for recommendations they would previously have researched
          themselves. The businesses being recommended mostly have no idea why, and the businesses
          being left out have no idea it's happening.
        </p>
        <p>
          Many of the things that influence whether a business can be understood and recommended are
          unglamorous and fixable: whether the AI systems can read your website, whether the facts
          about your business agree with each other across the web, and whether anything you've
          published actually answers the questions customers ask. Almost no small firm has had this
          looked at. That is the work Wardith does, at prices a small business can justify.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--tint">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="split" style="margin-bottom: 3rem;">
        <div data-reveal>
          <h2>How do we work?</h2>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="stages">
          <div class="stage" data-reveal>
            <div class="stage-head">
              <h3>Plainly</h3>
            </div>
            <div class="stage-body">
              <p>
                We write reports in ordinary English, we price in round numbers, and we tell you
                when you don't need us. Our audit exists partly so we can say "you're fine" and mean
                it.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="stage" data-reveal>
            <div class="stage-head">
              <h3>Honestly about uncertainty</h3>
            </div>
            <div class="stage-body">
              <p>
                Nobody controls what an AI assistant says. We work on the inputs we can observe and
                influence, and we measure what happens, but we separate what we can demonstrate
                from what we're inferring. We don't show numbers that can't be checked.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="stage" data-reveal>
            <div class="stage-head">
              <h3>In the open</h3>
            </div>
            <div class="stage-body">
              <p>
                This website is built with the same methods we sell. Everything on it is readable by
                the AI crawlers, the facts are stated in machine-readable form, and the FAQ answers
                real questions. If the approach works, you'll be able to see it working on us.
              </p>
              <p>
                And we'd rather you checked than took our word for it. We've published
                <a href="/ask-your-ai/">the prompts for interrogating this business</a>, and any
                other provider you're weighing up, along with the audit we ran on ourselves before
                selling one to anybody.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--invert">
    <div class="wrap split">
      <div data-reveal>
        <h2>Who's behind it?</h2>
        {
          business.founderPhoto && (
            <figure class="founder-photo">
              <img
                src={business.founderPhoto}
                alt={business.founder}
                width="880"
                height="1100"
                loading="lazy"
                decoding="async"
              />
            </figure>
          )
        }
      </div>
      <div>
        <div data-reveal>
          <p>
            Wardith is run by {business.founder}, from {business.basedIn}. One person does the work.
            When you email Wardith, you're emailing him, and the report you get back is one he wrote.
          </p>
          <p>
            Kieran spent eight years in operations at {business.founderFormerEmployer}, making
            sure containers were sent and arrived as planned. That work is mostly about keeping
            information accurate and consistent across systems that don't naturally agree, and
            noticing when one of them is quietly wrong — which turns out to be a large part of what
            this work is too.
            {
              business.founderLinkedIn && (
                <>
                  {' '}The full work history is on <a href={business.founderLinkedIn}>LinkedIn</a>.
                </>
              )
            }
          </p>
          <p>
            He came across this problem by chance while building a few websites: the gap between
            what a business publishes about itself and what an AI assistant actually believes about
            it. Rather than assume, he started testing it properly — the same question put to
            several assistants, repeatedly, and the answers written down. The first business he ran
            the finished method on was his own. It failed badly enough that the company changed its
            name, and Wardith was built around the method rather than the other way round.
            <a href="/ask-your-ai/self-audit/">Read the audit that led to the name change</a>.
          </p>
          {
            !business.founderLinkedIn && (
              <p class="flag">
                [PLACEHOLDER: LinkedIn profile URL — set `founderLinkedIn` in
                src/data/business.ts. It links here and joins the structured data as `sameAs`.]
              </p>
            )
          }
          {
            !business.founderPhoto && (
              <p class="flag">
                [PLACEHOLDER: founder photograph — add the file to site/public and set
                `founderPhoto` in src/data/business.ts.]
              </p>
            )
          }
          <p>
            Wardith is available to clients across the {business.areaServedLabel}, and the work is
            done remotely — there's nothing about it that needs us in the same room.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <Statement cite="Everything is agreed in writing, so there's a record of what was promised.">
        Small enough that you always know <em>who did the work.</em>
      </Statement>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
